<title>PERU: Peru bank liquidity rises 8.85 percent in 1st half.</title>
<headline>Peru bank liquidity rises 8.85 percent in 1st half.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1997-08-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Peru's total banking system liquidity rose 8.85 percent in the first half of 1997 to stand at 34.153 billion soles, compared with 31.376 billion soles at the end of 1996, the Central Reserve Bank said Monday.</p>
<p>During June, liquidity rose 1.05 percent, or 355 million soles, the bank said in its weekly bulletin.</p>
<p>Liquidity in 1996 rose 38.26 percent from 22.694 billion soles at the close of 1995.</p>
<p>((--Saul Hudson, Lima Newsroom 511 221-2134))</p>
